            <ArticleTitle>A Rare Presentation of Paraovarian Sclerosing Stromal Tumor with High Mitotic Activity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e13-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jpag.2015.08.007</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1083-3188(15)00308-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Sclerosing stromal tumor is an extremely rare type of benign ovarian sex cord stromal tumor.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE" NlmCategory="METHODS">The benign characteristic of this tumor is well known but we present an uncommon case of paraovarian sclerosing stromal tumor with high mitotic activity.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS AND CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Despite this potential malignancy, our patient was treated successfully with enucleation only.</AbstractText>
